From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kebab refactor <kebab@local.invalid>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 01:38:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dp: don't apply the wide-bus pixel-clock halving to
 link bandwidth

msm_dp_bridge_mode_valid() halves mode_pclk_khz when wide bus or YUV420
is in use and then reuses that halved value both for the controller's
pixel-clock ceiling and for the link bandwidth check.

Only the first is correct. Wide bus is a DPU-internal datapath width: it
carries two pixels per clock so the datapath can run at half the rate.
The DP link is unaffected -- every pixel still crosses the wire at the
same rate. Using the halved clock for the bandwidth comparison makes the
validator twice as optimistic as the hardware for every non-YUV420 mode,
so modes that cannot fit are advertised, link training succeeds, and the
sink shows a black screen with no error anywhere.

Keep the original clock for msm_dp_panel_get_mode_bpp() and the
mode_rate_khz computation.

Observed on sm8250 (OnePlus 8T) with a 4K60 monitor over USB-C DP
altmode.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c | 15 +++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
index dc6f33809..228993fd7 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
@@ -698,6 +698,7 @@ enum drm_mode_status msm_dp_bridge_mode_valid(struct drm_bridge *bridge,
 	u32 mode_rate_khz = 0, supported_rate_khz = 0, mode_bpp = 0;
 	struct msm_dp *dp;
 	int mode_pclk_khz = mode->clock;
+	int link_pclk_khz = mode->clock;
 
 	dp = to_dp_bridge(bridge)->msm_dp_display;
 
@@ -709,6 +710,16 @@ enum drm_mode_status msm_dp_bridge_mode_valid(struct drm_bridge *bridge,
 	msm_dp_display = container_of(dp, struct msm_dp_display_private, msm_dp_display);
 	link_info = &msm_dp_display->panel->link_info;
 
+	/*
+	 * Wide bus halves the rate the DPU datapath runs at by carrying two
+	 * pixels per clock, so it applies to the controller's pixel-clock
+	 * ceiling checked just below. It does NOT halve what the DP link has
+	 * to carry: every pixel still crosses the wire. Keep the unhalved
+	 * clock for the link bandwidth arithmetic, or this validator is 2x
+	 * optimistic for every non-YUV420 mode and advertises modes the link
+	 * cannot drive -- link training then succeeds and the sink shows a
+	 * black screen.
+	 */
 	if ((drm_mode_is_420_only(&dp->connector->display_info, mode) &&
 	     msm_dp_display->panel->vsc_sdp_supported) ||
 	     msm_dp_wide_bus_available(dp))
@@ -722,9 +733,9 @@ enum drm_mode_status msm_dp_bridge_mode_valid(struct drm_bridge *bridge,
 		mode_bpp = default_bpp;
 
 	mode_bpp = msm_dp_panel_get_mode_bpp(msm_dp_display->panel,
-			mode_bpp, mode_pclk_khz);
+			mode_bpp, link_pclk_khz);
 
-	mode_rate_khz = mode_pclk_khz * mode_bpp;
+	mode_rate_khz = link_pclk_khz * mode_bpp;
 	supported_rate_khz = link_info->num_lanes * link_info->rate * 8;
 
 	if (mode_rate_khz > supported_rate_khz)
